      "writtenOn": "2022-08-31T02:28:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think build orchestrator does not have the right granularity for this, and this should be done by the inner build system (Soong/Bazel)\n\ne.g. consider the API domain analysis of system. The build orchestrator has two choices\n1. Mount/Link/Cp the generated Android.bp files of Public API surface\n2. Not do the above\n3. (Selectively) Mount/Link/Cp the Android.bp files of cc_api_library but not the corresponding cc_api_headers \n\n1. If build orchestrator does option 1, all core module variants will link against `libc_headers.apiimport` (including source libc)\n2. If build orchestrator does option 2, system_apps that set sdk_version will get a missing module error (since e.g. libc from public API surface does not exist)\n3. Option 3 works I think, but also requires that we generate separate Android.bp files for cc_api_library and cc_api_headers\n\n(Kiyoung please correct me if I misunderstood this)\n\nI think the correct dependency resolution becomes more feasible once we tag each module variant with the API domain they belong to (which is what joeo@ is working on currently). I am ok with deferring this to a later date.",
      "parentUuid": "c0ad9edd_d2144ceb",
